<?xml version="1.0"?>
<Container version="2">
  <Name>pinebridge-tunnel</Name>
  <Repository>cloudflare/cloudflared:latest</Repository>
  <Registry>https://hub.docker.com/r/cloudflare/cloudflared</Registry>
  <Network>bridge</Network>
  <MyIP/>
  <Shell>sh</Shell>
  <Privileged>false</Privileged>
  <Support>https://forums.unraid.net/topic/200736-support-jakeshake-pinebridge-tradingview-alerts-%E2%86%92-metatrader-5/</Support>
  <Project>https://github.com/jakeshake/pinebridge</Project>
  <Overview>Pinebridge: TradingView alerts to MetaTrader 5. Send TradingView alerts straight to MetaTrader 5 on your own Unraid server. No paid signal-relay service, no VPS. This optional container is a Cloudflare Tunnel connector that exposes the pinebridge-bridge webhook to the internet with a stable HTTPS URL and no port-forwarding. Create the tunnel and token in the Cloudflare Zero Trust dashboard first -- see docs/cloudflare-tunnel-setup.md in the Pinebridge repo. Skip it if you already run a Cloudflare tunnel. Places real trades automatically: read the risk notice (https://github.com/jakeshake/pinebridge/blob/main/DISCLAIMER.md) and test on a demo account first.</Overview>
  <Description>Pinebridge: TradingView alerts to MetaTrader 5. Send TradingView alerts straight to MetaTrader 5 on your own Unraid server. No paid signal-relay service, no VPS. This optional container is a Cloudflare Tunnel connector that exposes the pinebridge-bridge webhook to the internet with a stable HTTPS URL and no port-forwarding. Create the tunnel and token in the Cloudflare Zero Trust dashboard first -- see docs/cloudflare-tunnel-setup.md in the Pinebridge repo. Skip it if you already run a Cloudflare tunnel. Places real trades automatically: read the risk notice (https://github.com/jakeshake/pinebridge/blob/main/DISCLAIMER.md) and test on a demo account first.</Description>
  <ReadMe>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jakeshake/pinebridge/main/README.md</ReadMe>
  <License>MIT</License>
  <ExtraSearchTerms>cloudflare tunnel cloudflared tradingview webhook pinebridge</ExtraSearchTerms>
  <Category>Network:Other</Category>
  <WebUI/>
  <TemplateURL>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jakeshake/pinebridge/main/extras/pinebridge-tunnel.template</TemplateURL>
  <Icon>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jakeshake/pinebridge/main/docs/icons/pinebridge-tunnel.png</Icon>
  <ExtraParams/>
  <PostArgs>tunnel run</PostArgs>
  <CPUset/>
  <DateInstalled/>
  <DonateText>If Pinebridge saves you a VPS or signal subscription, consider buying me a coffee.</DonateText>
  <DonateLink>https://buymeacoffee.com/jakeshake</DonateLink>
  <Requires>Create a tunnel in the Cloudflare Zero Trust dashboard and point its public hostname at http://[your Unraid IP]:5080 (the pinebridge-bridge WebUI Port) before starting this container. Optional: skip this container if you already run a Cloudflare tunnel -- just add a public hostname to it.</Requires>
  <Config Name="TUNNEL_TOKEN" Target="TUNNEL_TOKEN" Default="" Mode="" Description="Token for the tunnel you created in the Cloudflare Zero Trust dashboard" Type="Variable" Display="always" Required="true" Mask="true"></Config>
</Container>
